<% content_for :title, "How it works — SceneCore" %>

<section class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-4">How it works</h1>
  <p class="text-neutral-400 mb-12">
    Use Spotify to get discovered. Use SceneCore to build your fan base.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-16">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">For bands</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        Create your band's page, bring your albums over from Spotify, publish
        posts for your followers, and keep everything about your relationship
        with your fans in one place.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">For fans</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        Discover bands, listen to their music, follow the ones you care about,
        and keep up with what they publish.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-2">Membership plans</h2>
  <p class="text-neutral-400 mb-8">
    Following a band is free. Membership is how a fan supports one band
    directly, month to month, and unlocks what that band shares with its
    members. Each membership belongs to a single band — you can be a Fan of
    one and a Core Member of another.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-8">
    <% [
         [ "fan", "Get closer to the band.", [
           "Exclusive band feed",
           "News before the general public",
           "Behind-the-scenes photos and short videos",
           "Selected demos and alternative versions",
           "Poll participation",
           "Fan badge and subscriber community access"
         ], false ],
         [ "supporter", "Support the music and follow its creation.", [
           "Early access to releases",
           "Complete demos and rehearsal recordings",
           "Composition and production journals",
           "Exclusive videos and streams",
           "Digital supporter credits",
           "Merchandise discounts"
         ], true ],
         [ "core_member", "Become part of the band's core group.", [
           "Private livestreams and Q&A sessions",
           "Rare archives and unreleased versions",
           "Priority access to tickets and limited products",
           "Higher discounts and a permanent supporter page",
           "Direct messages to the band",
           "A say in decisions the band opens up"
         ], false ]
       ].each do |level, promise, benefits, highlighted| %>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border <%= highlighted ? "border-yellow-500/60" : "border-neutral-800" %> bg-neutral-900/60 p-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white"><%= level.humanize.titleize %></h3>
          <p class="mt-1">
            <span class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white">$<%= Membership::PRICES_IN_CENTS.fetch(level) / 100 %></span>
            <span class="text-sm text-neutral-500">/month per band</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400 italic">&ldquo;<%= promise %>&rdquo;</p>

        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm text-neutral-300">
          <% unless level == "fan" %>
            <li class="text-neutral-500">Everything in <%= level == "supporter" ? "Fan" : "Supporter" %>, plus:</li>
          <% end %>
          <% benefits.each do |benefit| %>
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span class="text-yellow-400" aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span><%= benefit %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mb-16">
    What each band actually publishes at every level is up to that band.
    Memberships renew monthly and can be cancelled at any time.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-2">The money side</h2>
  <p class="text-neutral-400 mb-8">
    We would rather be plain about this than make you guess.
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-12">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Creating a band page is free</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        There is no monthly fee for bands. You create your page, publish your
        music and content, and build your fan base without paying to be here.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Following is free for fans</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        You only pay if you choose to become a member of a band, and you pay
        that band — one membership at a time, for as long as you want it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Bands keep 75% of memberships</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        Of every membership payment, 75% goes to the band and 25% to SceneCore.
        That share covers running the platform: hosting the music and content,
        handling payments, and keeping the band's home online.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Bands keep 75% of store sales</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        The same split applies when a band sells merchandise through its store:
        75% goes to the band and 25% to SceneCore. It happens automatically when
        the payment is made, so there is nothing to reconcile afterwards.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 p-6">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-2">Payments run through Stripe</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        Card details are handled by Stripe and never touch SceneCore's servers.
        Bands selling products connect their own Stripe account, so store
        earnings go straight to them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <% unless user_signed_in? %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Join Now", new_user_registration_path, class: "rounded-full bg-yellow-400 text-black font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:bg-yellow-300 transition" %>
      <%= link_to "Browse bands", discover_bands_path, class: "rounded-full border border-neutral-700 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:border-neutral-500 transition" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
